{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1255 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7e1ba3f5f5c2771f6399e9bf464681905acd4fe22efc9df5fac5acd3d96ab847" :edb/db-before-t 1254 :edb/db-after-t 1255 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534567 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:12:40.956Z" 13194139534567 true] [17592186129051 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295860 13194139534567 true] [17592186129051 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295888 13194139534567 true] [17592186129051 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295891 13194139534567 true] [17592186129051 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295901 13194139534567 true] [17592186129054 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295894 13194139534567 true] [17592186129054 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295915 13194139534567 true] [17592186129189 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295867 13194139534567 true] [17592186129189 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295874 13194139534567 true] [17592186129190 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295881 13194139534567 true] [17592186129190 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295908 13194139534567 true] [17592186129576 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534567 true] [17592186129576 1100 "For the first year of a newborn's life, its height $H$ increases at a rate that is proportional to the time, in months, since birth.\n\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the height of the baby at time $t$?" 13194139534567 false] [17592186129576 1100 "For the first year of a newborn's life, its height $H$ increases at a rate that is proportional to the time, in months, since birth.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the height of the baby at time $t?$" 13194139534567 true] [17592186129576 1145 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*For the first year of a newborn's life, its **height** $H$ **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **time**, in months, since birth.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *time* since birth. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295860 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295861 13194139534567 true] [17592186295860 1089 "q-119052" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295860 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534567 true] [17592186295860 1100 "Tommy drinks $5$ milliliters of vitamin syrup each day from a bottle. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the amount of vitamin syrup $S$ (in milliliters) remaining in the bottle? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in days." 13194139534567 true] [17592186295860 1113 #uuid "1f1906d2-5133-52e7-99dc-75f54ead86d2" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295860 1145 "If the amount of vitamin syrup remaining is $S$ milliliters, then the rate of change of the syrup volume is $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince Tommy drinks $5$ milliliters of syrup each day, the rate of change of the amount of syrup remaining is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the amount of syrup is *decreasing*." 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295862 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295863 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295864 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295865 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295866 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1041 "selection" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186295863 13194139534567 true] [17592186295861 1110 #uuid "94ea4618-9dc5-548a-b85a-b4f9a69dc59f" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295862 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295862 1111 #uuid "452ce28e-0228-58ef-abad-de2089e6ffe6" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295863 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295863 1111 #uuid "fa86354b-b7d0-5914-b45a-4ca47137e0f1" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295864 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5t" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295864 1111 #uuid "51eff358-2390-532f-98da-b66e94258aaf" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295865 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=5" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295865 1111 #uuid "a035a897-48f4-559e-91de-9a87d4030048" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295866 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5S" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295866 1111 #uuid "799bfcb6-3708-5802-9f4a-57f4cb9791ba" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295867 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295868 13194139534567 true] [17592186295867 1089 "q-143035" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295867 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534567 true] [17592186295867 1100 "During a certain chemical reaction, the volume of gas $G$ increases with time. The rate of change of the volume of gas is proportional to the square of the time $t,$ in seconds, since the reaction started. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of gas at time $t?$" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295867 1113 #uuid "116a80ae-5b7a-5a13-919a-314322a246f1" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295867 1145 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*During a certain chemical reaction, the **volume** of gas $G$ **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the volume of gas is **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t,$ in seconds.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume of gas* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *square of the time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}∝{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume of gas *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295869 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295870 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295871 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295872 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295873 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1041 "selection" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1104 #edb/ref 17592186295871 13194139534567 true] [17592186295868 1110 #uuid "b79b0e9e-ce07-5367-ae03-a5fb5855bf88" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295869 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295869 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295869 1111 #uuid "68b74365-7af7-533c-a4b6-82b95ad8c598" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295870 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295870 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295870 1111 #uuid "4dac0845-ece5-5c93-ac78-e3107df5c303" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295871 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295871 1111 #uuid "978ca961-fc0f-5ab9-9bc4-26f6aa707375" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295872 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-kt,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295872 1111 #uuid "b49dba43-1fc2-53b2-b7f9-3b4142fab53c" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295873 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295873 1111 #uuid "3e965958-eaee-5339-9cf7-a5c18c0224a3" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295874 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295875 13194139534567 true] [17592186295874 1089 "q-143036" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295874 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534567 true] [17592186295874 1100 "The velocity $v$ of a stone falling through some water to the bottom of a lake decreases with time. The rate of change of the stone's velocity is proportional to the square of the velocity. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the velocity at time $t?$" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295874 1113 #uuid "000bf12e-faf9-50f0-869d-67748f8e8824" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295874 1145 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **velocity** $v$ of a stone falling through some water to the bottom of a lake **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the stone's velocity is **proportional** to the **square of the velocity**.  *\n\nWe note the following: \n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *velocity* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *velocity squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}∝{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the velocity *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-k{v}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295876 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295877 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295878 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295879 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295880 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1041 "selection" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1104 #edb/ref 17592186295877 13194139534567 true] [17592186295875 1110 #uuid "27ffd44f-d95c-5b66-9de7-8b47da4773de" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295876 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{v},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295876 1111 #uuid "6a4c60a8-f101-5eef-9c93-587751322eb0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295877 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295877 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295877 1111 #uuid "63a1febe-6a7a-5422-8c17-c5540c2e7e97" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295878 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295878 1111 #uuid "9188262e-9673-5eed-83b2-a5fd5cd3b6d0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295879 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{v}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534567 true] [17592186295879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534567 true] [17592186295879 1111 #uuid "